{title:Title}

{p 8 17 2}
{bf:latexedu} -- LaTeX beginner's learning program: installation and basics

{title:Syntax}

{p 8 13 2}
{cmd:latexedu} [{cmd:install} {cmd:basic} {cmd:example} {cmd:all}]

{title:Description}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:latexedu} is an entry-level learning program for LaTeX beginners,
published by Dingyuan Accounting, which follows the academic principle of
{bf:scientific and standardized, humane and good}. In three short lessons
it helps you get to know LaTeX quickly: Overleaf or a local installation,
the document skeleton and basic commands, and a ready-to-compile Chinese
paper template.

{p 4 4 2}
With no options, {cmd:latexedu} displays all three lessons in turn. Use the
options to review a single lesson at any time.

{title:Options}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:install} displays only lesson 1: Overleaf online and TeX Live/MiKTeX local installation.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:basic} displays only lesson 2: the document skeleton, sections, math formulas, tables, and figures.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:example} displays only lesson 3: a complete Chinese paper template.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:all} displays all three lessons (the default).

{title:Examples}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. latexedu}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays all three lessons.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. latexedu, install}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays only the installation steps.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. latexedu, example}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays only the Chinese paper template.

{title:Remarks}

{p 4 4 2}
{bf:Learning tips}

{p 4 8 2}
1. Run {cmd:latexedu} and read all three lessons first.

{p 4 8 2}
2. Practice online with Overleaf: no installation, instant preview, ideal for beginners.

{p 4 8 2}
3. For Chinese documents, always compile with XeLaTeX and load the ctex package.

{p 4 8 2}
4. Memorize the skeleton first, then add content block by block.

{p 4 4 2}
{bf:Dingyuan Accounting} adheres to the principle of
{bf:scientific and standardized, humane and good} and hopes every beginner
learns with joy.

